name c02m02-masquerade
timeout 300
time 1998-10-14T05:00:00Z

# DELTA FORCE (NovaLogic 1998), CAMPAIGN ONE "PERU", FILE SLOT C02M02, PLAY ORDER 5 OF 6 --
# {Masquerade}, working title "C02M02 - Steal Radio Book", Objective CALM [BMS]. TWO predecessors,
# Flood and Bad Habit -- the campaign is a graph, not a list [CAMP].
# Spec and provenance: mods/delta-force/doc/. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [CAMP]: "Infiltrate the mercenary base-camp, designated Objective Calm, and steal a copy of
# the enemy's encryption codebook." M02SUBGOAL01 "Retrieve the code book from Objective Calm." +
# M02SUBGOAL02 "Reach the extraction point." FAIL M02SUBFAIL01 "Black Widow is eliminated."
# THE RADIO [DLG]: "Proceed east and obtain enemy code book." + "Do so without alerting the enemy to
# your presence." + "Proceed to extraction point."
# THE FIELD [BMS]: 725 objects, 1537 x 1186 m, IP (-645.3,-545.0), enemy centroid (-283.0,-483.8) =
# 367 m at 080 deg = "east". C2M2.TRN "Death & More Death", NIGHT preset [TRN] -- which is what the
# briefing's "the need for absolute stealth" and the radio's "without alerting" are made of.
# THE CAST: 33 hostiles -> lattice pitch 235.0 m, the campaign's thinnest - Objective Calm, the tent
# group (`tent, netting` + `tent, long` + 2x `tent, small`) as ONE neutral object at (-139.1,-522.7) -
# two abandoned villages, 7 parts at (-765.9,-227.8) and 4 parts at (-715.5,-832.9), one object each
# (D5); their 692.7 m at 295 deg from the objective is the measurement that agrees with the briefing's
# "690m northwest" to 3 m and proves the metre a second time - and ZERO friendly soldiers, matching
# "no other team members have been assigned to this operation" [CAMP]. campaign.md 10 states the
# consequence as a test: any friendly unit here is a mod defect. The one friendly-team object is the
# Black Widow, which is not a team member but the extraction asset.
# THREE THINGS THIS FILE CANNOT SAY, AND ONE IT CAN SAY EXACTLY:
#   `Carrying: Code Book` [GAME] is a HUD state the unit model has no slot for, so goal 1 degrades
#   from RETRIEVE to OVERFLY -- the objective becomes a waypoint on Objective Calm.
#   The Black Widow's coordinate was not recorded, so it stands on the IP, like Weatherman's EP.
#   The extraction leg is 506.7 m, i.e. barely more than the 500 m capture radius (D4).
#   What it CAN say exactly is the stealth constraint: "without alerting the enemy" is
#   `objective no_fire`, and this is the only mission of the four mods where a briefing sentence maps
#   onto an objective keyword with no loss at all. So `bravo2` carries NO ordnance and flies
#   `set task route`.
#
# READING RULE (binding), and it is the sharpest one here because the file can go GREEN. campaign.md
# 10: three ways to fail and one to pass -- no codebook, no extraction, or Black Widow destroyed.
# exit 0 is REACHABLE and it is the emptiest result in the campaign: it proves that the substitute can
# fly 1.5 km without firing, which is every property of Masquerade except the mission. Read exit 0
# here as a measurement of the FORMAT (three goals expressed, one of them exactly), never of the
# simulation. An exit other than 0 is the interesting outcome and must be reported with its cause.

# ---- THE NINE DISCLOSURES. Full text in c02m01-insurrection.fbm; in force here unchanged.
#   D1 no man on foot: Bravo Two flies as `f16`, 300 kt vs a 1.4 m/s walk, 150 m vs a 1.7 m eye, no
#      posture, no ground LOS, no cover - D2 the hostile soldier is a `target_soft` and cannot shoot
#      (measured: ground vs ground = 0 weapon events) - D3 the rifle has no target (gun bundles resolve
#      against aircraft only); 2 satchel charges -> 2 x `mk82` - D4 the waypoint capture radius is
#      500 m and not tunable, which is wider than four of six missions' whole ingress - D5 the N
#      hostiles are a lattice on the measured centroid at pitch sqrt(EW*NS/N); count, centroid and
#      areal density measured, arrangement reconstructed - D6 `--elev const`, flat 0 m, though fb-tiles
#      does cover Peru (629.30-688.72 m at the six box centres) - D7 the striker spawns 3 000 m out on
#      the bearing to its aim point, outside the mission box - D8 one striker is one aim point, and it
#      is also ONE RELEASE: 2 x mk82 declared, 1 fired, in every armed file - D9 date 1998-10-13 [MAN],
#      instant checked against the runner's own CLOCK line.

# MEASURED (exit 0, `--elev const`, `--threads 1/2/4` byte-identical): THE EMPTY GREEN, EXACTLY AS THE
# READING RULE PREDICTS.
#   t = 0.0 s    CLOCK sunElDeg -73.05 -- the .TRN night preset, checked
#   t = 14.7 s   wp0 `by=capture` -- Objective Calm, the tent group, i.e. "the codebook"
#   t = 14.8 s   wp1 `by=capture` -- the extraction point, 506.7 m away, 0.1 s later (D4)
#   t = 300.1 s  all three objectives met: `waypoints`, `no_fire`, `protect unit blackwidow`
#   weapons      ZERO releases, ZERO gun events, no ordnance carried at all
#   verdict      SUCCESS. What that proves: the format can state all three of this mission's
#                conditions, and one of them -- "without alerting the enemy" -> `objective no_fire` --
#                is the only briefing sentence in the four NovaLogic mods that maps onto an objective
#                keyword with NO loss. What it does not prove: anything about infiltration, stealth,
#                night, or a codebook, none of which exist here.

unit bravo2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn -8.72739 -76.18199 150 227.5 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  set gun_rounds 30
  set cmds_mode off
  set task route
  wp -8.74560 -76.20209 150 300
  wp -8.74252 -76.19869 150 300
  objective waypoints
  objective no_fire
  objective protect unit blackwidow

